WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:51.280
[Music]

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:57.730
[Narrator:] Rat killing combined with basic
measures of ratproofing and sanitation

00:00:57.730 --> 00:01:04.829
constitutes a major step in permanent rat
control, but rat killing by itself does not

00:01:04.829 --> 00:01:08.170
result in permanent rat control.

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:13.640
So long as food sources and harborage remain
undisturbed, killing rats merely

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:17.020
lessens competition for those that survive.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:27.430
With less competition, rapid reproduction
rebuilds the population.

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:31.370
Soon, the infestation is as great as ever.

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:41.140
When a building has been ratproofed to keep
rats out, it is possible to eliminate all

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:44.630
rats within the premises by the techniques of rat killing.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:51.920
It is the rat eradicator's job to get rid
of every last rat remaining in the premises.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:56.850
One surviving pregnant female might cause
a re-infestation that would completely

00:01:56.850 --> 00:02:00.979
nullify the effort and expense of ratproofing.

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:17.930
The tools of rat killing are various rodenticides
and mechanical devices.

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:23.290
The selection and use of these tools depends
upon the area to be made rat-free.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:34.240
For instance, in this rat-proofed restaurant
kitchen, no chances should be taken with

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:39.379
the poison that rats might spread to human food.

00:02:39.379 --> 00:02:44.230
In this case, red squill is selected as the
rodenticide.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:49.879
Red squill is relatively safe around humans
and most domestic animals, since it is in itself

00:02:49.879 --> 00:02:55.090
an emetic and is normally regurgitated before
lasting harm is done.

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:59.400
But the rat cannot regurgitate and retains
the poison.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:04.480
For this reason, red squill is the most commonly
used rodenticide.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:08.599
But the problem is to get the rat to eat the
red squill.

00:03:08.599 --> 00:03:13.879
Red squill is bitter; therefore, it must be
mixed with food that is highly acceptable to rats.

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:19.930
A poison bait is prepared of fresh, lean ground beef

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:23.070
and chicken mash mixed with red squill.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:31.360
Salad oil is added as a binder.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:43.880
The mixture is prepared in small amounts called
torpedoes for distribution to the rats.

00:03:54.129 --> 00:03:59.949
An alternate cereal poison bait is prepared
of steamed rolled oats, ground bacon, and red squill.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:06.379
Experience has shown that better results are
obtained if a choice of food baits

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:08.739
is offered to the rats.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.980
Again salad oil is used as a binder.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:24.800
The preparation must be made attractive to
the prospective customer.

00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:35.410
The cereal and meat base are wrapped in contrasting paper so that the eradication man

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:42.099
can distinguish one from the other and thus can learn which bait the rats prefer.

00:04:42.099 --> 00:04:46.630
The poisoned baits must be placed where the
rats can easily find them.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:49.770
It would be too much to expect the rats to
search for them.

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:57.440
Bait is placed along runways and near customary
sources of food.

00:04:58.629 --> 00:05:03.229
To kill as many rats as possible before they
develop an aversion to the poison,

00:05:03.229 --> 00:05:05.589
a generous supply of bait is used.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:10.319
Rats seek food where they have previously
found it.

00:05:10.319 --> 00:05:16.149
They are usually suspicious of any change.
However, in the absence of their regular food,

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:20.129
hunger will induce them to accept any food
they can find.

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:29.540
Rats in the open are normally nibblers and
samplers.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:34.270
They usually eat a full meal only in the safety
of their harborage.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:38.520
For this reason the torpedoes are made in
a convenient size for the rats

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.620
to carry away for later eating.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:58.480
Each torpedo contains enough rodenticide so
that if later it is shared by two or three

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:02.690
other rats, each rat will receive a lethal
dose.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:11.779
Red squill takes from 24 to 72 hours to kill.

00:06:11.779 --> 00:06:17.279
When a rat has eaten red squill, it usually
becomes lethargic in one to two hours.

00:06:17.279 --> 00:06:23.599
Four to 14 hours later, characteristic tremors
begin, followed by progressive paralysis.

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:27.620
If it can, the rat will return to its harborage.

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:30.980
Thus death usually occurs in the nest.

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:40.139
Since up to 90 percent of all rats poisoned
with red squill tend to die in their nests

00:06:40.139 --> 00:06:45.199
or in secluded places, it is difficult to
determine how many rats have been killed.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:57.400
A checkup in the restaurant kitchen two days
after setting out the poison reveals lessened

00:06:57.409 --> 00:07:02.819
rat activity, but definite odor of dead rat
coming from behind the stove

00:07:02.819 --> 00:07:06.259
guides the eradication man to one of the rat
casualties.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:34.479
Hmmm...another rat, dead before it could get
to its nest.

00:07:34.479 --> 00:07:38.639
Judging from the smell, there must be still
another rat in the hole.

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:54.120
Unfortunately, it is out of reach in the double
wall.

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:04.370
Ripping out the wall would be expensive.

00:08:04.449 --> 00:08:11.289
The best thing to do is to cover the odor
with a masking agent such as isoborneol acetate.

00:08:11.289 --> 00:08:13.270
Have all the rats been killed?

00:08:13.270 --> 00:08:16.270
That's hardly likely.

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:21.520
The best way of finding out whether any rats are still living is to put down some patches of talc

00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:28.179
or porathalite, or 10 percent DDT dust, to
make rat tracks easily visible.

00:08:28.179 --> 00:08:34.279
A patch of approximately 12 by 18 inches and
about 1/8 inch thick is spread

00:08:34.279 --> 00:08:37.169
and smoothed with a straight edge.

00:08:37.169 --> 00:08:41.269
Smoothing will make it easier to see the tracks
clearly.

00:08:41.269 --> 00:08:46.720
Because rat signs age slowly, it is impossible
to tell from them the progress

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:49.379
of day-to-day eradication.

00:08:49.379 --> 00:08:55.550
The tracking patch is the best way of determining the extent of rat activity during a given night.

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:00.329
The tracking patches are laid along the rats' principle routes

00:09:00.329 --> 00:09:03.660
between food, water, and harborage.

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:09.670
In view of the rats limited home range, patches must be so placed that every rat present

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:12.839
will traverse some patch during the night.

00:09:12.839 --> 00:09:16.139
Too few patches, or patches poorly or patches poorly placed,

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:19.500
can give a false impression that all rats have been killed.

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:31.079
Early the next morning the patches are examined with a flashlight

00:09:31.079 --> 00:09:33.350
before the kitchen is cleaned for use.

00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:37.410
The first patch is smooth.

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:43.500
This patch clearly shows tracks of several
rats.

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:47.210
The flashlight is held at an angle of about
30 degrees to the floor

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:50.660
so as to throw into relief the impressions in the dust.

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:56.910
Obviously the job is not completed yet, and
by now the surviving rats

00:09:56.910 --> 00:10:00.230
have probably developed an aversion to red
squill.

00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:05.230
Therefore, the rat control man decides to
use Antu to complete the kill.

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:12.040
Antu is unique in that it can be used as a
tracking poison.

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:17.170
The control man removes the old patches in
order to avoid diluting the Antu mixture.

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:24.740
Antu is specific for Norway rats, while roof
rats have a high tolerance for it.

00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:30.820
Next, the control man lays down new patches consisting of a mixture of 20 percent Antu dust

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:34.080
and 80 percent pyrophyllite.

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:40.800
Even though expensive, Antu is economical
when used under ideal conditions.

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:46.149
In this case, the rats have become accustomed
to tracking patches in their runways.

00:10:46.149 --> 00:10:53.669
It is virtually certain that the rats will
come into contact with the rodenticide.

00:10:56.380 --> 00:11:01.100
In their search for food, the rats run through
the Antu dust.

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:05.790
The dust irritates the rats' paws, causing
them later to lick their paws,

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:08.430
thus ingesting the Antu dust.

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:22.519
Antu causes an over-production of liquid in
the rat's lungs.

00:11:22.519 --> 00:11:26.819
Within 48 hours the rat dies as though by
drowning.

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:36.300
When no rat tracks appear on the tracking
patches for five nights,

00:11:36.310 --> 00:11:40.730
the eradication man knows the restaurant kitchen
has been freed of rats.

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:49.640
Rats may re-enter a rat-free and rat-proof
building through an open door

00:11:49.649 --> 00:11:51.920
or with merchandise deliveries.

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:57.420
To maintain the kitchen in a rat-free condition,
frequent inspection is necessary.

00:11:57.720 --> 00:12:01.620
Inspection must be at regularly scheduled
intervals so as to find

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:04.790
any re-infestation as soon as possible.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:16.540
Sometimes the rodenticide selected does not
work too well.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:21.399
In this fish market, torpedoes containing
red squill bait have been tried,

00:12:21.399 --> 00:12:23.899
but for some reason have proved ineffective.

00:12:23.899 --> 00:12:27.379
The surviving rats will no longer take the
red squill bait,

00:12:27.379 --> 00:12:29.699
having developed an aversion to it.

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:41.920
Since the rats have been feeding mainly on
fish and fish scraps,

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:45.800
the eradicator decides to use arsenic trioxide in a fish bait.

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:56.730
The arsenic trioxide is added to an emetic,
in this case tartar emetic, and weighed carefully.

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:04.689
The tarter emetic is intended to protect animals
other than rats by causing them

00:13:04.689 --> 00:13:07.229
to vomit the poison.

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:22.350
The poison and emetic is added to the
fish.

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:27.220
Finally, the bait is prepared in torpedoes.

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:40.240
As an alternate bait, ground bread crumbs
and ground bacon are mixed

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:45.079
with the finely powered emetic and the arsenic
trioxide.

00:13:57.400 --> 00:14:00.740
[Narrator:] This second bait is made into
torpedoes.

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:05.640
Again, contrasting paper is used to distinguish
them from the other bait.

00:14:13.899 --> 00:14:17.799
In the fish market, these poisoned baits are
readily taken by the rats.

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:30.480
Arsenic trioxide is a poison which is absorbed
into the rat's intestinal tract

00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:37.480
causing gastroenteritis, destruction of kidneys,
exhaustion, and generalized paralysis.

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:41.620
Death usually occurs in less than 24 hours,
although in a few cases

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:45.880
where minimal lethal doses are eaten, it
may take up to six days.

00:15:00.220 --> 00:15:05.240
To check on the possibility of any rat surviving,
tracking patches are put down.

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:12.019
In this case, the patch is laid in a 15 inch
radius around the rat hole, making it impossible

00:15:12.019 --> 00:15:17.089
for any rat using the hole to avoid leaving
its tracks in the patch.

00:15:17.089 --> 00:15:21.889
Thus, well-placed tracking patches offer a
check on the effectiveness

00:15:21.889 --> 00:15:23.849
of any specific treatment.

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:37.629
In addition to indicating the presence or
absence of rats, tracks found in such

00:15:37.629 --> 00:15:44.560
patches often indicate the size of surviving
rats and the number of rats using the runway.

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:48.880
Such tracks are also a clue to the direction
and purpose of rat travel.

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:58.899
Only when an adequate number of properly placed
tracking patches are free from rat footprints

00:15:58.899 --> 00:16:04.190
for five nights in succession can the premises
be considered rat free.

00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:10.520
A quick-acting, highly toxic rodenticide such
as 1080 water can be used

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:16.120
only when the premises can be effectively closed off
to humans and animal pets.

00:16:16.129 --> 00:16:21.379
When the area contains food, it is necessary
to cut off all sources of water,

00:16:21.379 --> 00:16:25.939
and rely on the rat's thirst to force them to take a water-borne poison.

00:16:25.939 --> 00:16:30.820
1080 water is placed in water-proof, non-spillable cups.

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:34.600
1080 is a very dangerous poison.

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:44.880
Only trained and experienced eradication men
should be permitted to use it.

00:16:55.089 --> 00:17:01.360
The utmost precautions must be taken whenever
1080 is used.

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:03.250
Rats must have water.

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:07.850
1080 water is tasteless, odorless, and quite
acceptable to them.

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:20.020
One swallow is a lethal dose.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:40.120
1080 kills within one-half to two hours.

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:44.510
For some unknown reason, a high percentage
of rats killed with 1080

00:17:44.510 --> 00:17:49.210
die in accessible places and are easily recovered.

00:17:59.020 --> 00:18:02.040
Convulsions precede death by heart failure.

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:34.520
[Narrator:] The next day, the first order
of business is to count, pick up,

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:38.320
and dispose of cups and carcasses.

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:43.800
Dead rats and every used 1080 cup should be
incinerated.

00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:49.060
Only licensed and qualified eradication men
should be permitted to use 1080,

00:18:49.070 --> 00:18:52.830
and then only under carefully supervised conditions.

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:11.920
With 1080 as with other rodenticides, tracking
patches are laid to determine

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:14.760
whether all the rats have been killed.

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:23.760
This basement storage room has been rat-proofed,
but colonies of rats

00:19:23.770 --> 00:19:27.289
still remain and have to be exterminated.

00:19:27.289 --> 00:19:32.610
The rat control man decides to try another
rat poison, warfarin.

00:19:32.610 --> 00:19:37.820
Warfarin was originally known as compound
42.

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:42.399
Strictly speaking, it is an anti-coagulant,causing
a slow bleeding to death.

00:19:42.399 --> 00:19:44.679
It is tasteless and odorless.

00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:54.880
One effective bait to use with warfarin is
cornmeal mixed with a discoloring agent

00:19:54.890 --> 00:19:58.690
such as activated charcoal to warn against
human use.

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:09.700
Warfarin mixed with yellow cornmeal and charcoal
is placed in a bait box

00:20:09.710 --> 00:20:12.279
near a rat entrance.

00:20:12.279 --> 00:20:17.100
The purpose of the bait box in this case is
not to prevent human access,

00:20:17.100 --> 00:20:20.400
but to avoid the poison being kicked and spilled
accidentally.

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:24.680
The use of such a bait box is optional.

00:20:24.690 --> 00:20:29.309
The box contains enough bait to last until
the next service date.

00:20:29.309 --> 00:20:34.590
A tracking patch is spread around the bait
box to indicate the presence or absence of rats.

00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:46.740
Another bait box is located near a place where
the rats have fed in the past.

00:20:46.750 --> 00:20:49.530
Tracking patches are placed around this box
also.

00:20:55.620 --> 00:21:00.640
During the night the rats are attracted by
the bait, and approach the box.

00:21:00.640 --> 00:21:05.200
As no other food is uncovered and easily available,
the rats investigate

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:08.440
and find the food to their liking.

00:21:08.440 --> 00:21:13.929
Unlike other poisons, warfarin does not create
an aversion in rats that eat it.

00:21:13.929 --> 00:21:17.539
They come back again and again.

00:21:17.539 --> 00:21:22.809
Rats often show a preference for warfarin
in cornmeal over other foods,

00:21:22.809 --> 00:21:25.009
even though the other is unpoisoned.

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:37.840
The next day, examination of the tracking
patch shows the rats' reactions to the bait.

00:21:40.570 --> 00:21:44.150
They have eaten so much that it's necessary
to replenish the supply.

00:21:49.250 --> 00:21:51.710
The effect of warfarin is cumulative.

00:21:51.710 --> 00:21:57.019
Repeated doses over a period of several days
will gradually weaken the rat

00:21:57.019 --> 00:21:58.719
by loss of blood.

00:22:04.010 --> 00:22:08.460
The rat usually dies between the fifth and
eighth day.

00:22:08.460 --> 00:22:13.900
The slow, cumulative effect of the poison
delays the rat's death for several days.

00:22:13.900 --> 00:22:20.400
Thus, warfarin is dangerous to domestic animals
only with repeated ingestion.

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:33.210
Despite its safety features, warfarin must
be used with caution, placed in a bait box,

00:22:33.210 --> 00:22:38.830
or in inaccessible locations where humans
and household pets cannot get at it.

00:22:41.000 --> 00:22:46.059
With warfarin, just as with all other rodenticides,
tracking patches are needed

00:22:46.059 --> 00:22:49.539
to indicate the presence or absence of surviving rats.

00:22:55.320 --> 00:23:01.660
For 10 days after the last rat was found dead,
there have been no tracks around the box.

00:23:01.660 --> 00:23:07.750
Yet, another patch near the rat entry hole
shows the tracks of more than one surviving rat.

00:23:08.920 --> 00:23:14.549
Since warfarin won't complete the job, the
bait boxes are removed,

00:23:14.549 --> 00:23:17.600
but the remaining rats must be killed.

00:23:17.600 --> 00:23:20.740
The eradicator decides to use steel traps.

00:23:20.740 --> 00:23:26.120
He selects one, carefully sets it at hair
trigger, and places it at an opening to rat harborage.

00:23:28.670 --> 00:23:33.960
Because the steel trap does not kill the rat
outright, it must be securely fastened

00:23:33.960 --> 00:23:36.560
so the rat cannot drag it to his harborage.

00:23:41.299 --> 00:23:48.090
To force the rat to cross the trap, the eradicator
puts a box on each side of the trap.

00:23:48.090 --> 00:23:53.010
The boxes are pushed back against the platform
to prevent the rat from turning aside

00:23:53.010 --> 00:23:54.830
to bypass the trap.

00:24:00.800 --> 00:24:05.179
After setting out sufficient traps, he puts
out additional tracking patches

00:24:05.179 --> 00:24:06.679
and smooths the old ones.

00:24:09.990 --> 00:24:14.870
The next morning, inspection shows that one rat has been caught in a trap and is still alive.

00:24:23.910 --> 00:24:30.059
Another trap has evidently been sprung and
dragged around but there is no rat in it.

00:24:30.059 --> 00:24:34.059
The tracking patch near the rat entry reveals a rat's footprints.

00:24:40.540 --> 00:24:45.740
Since the eradicator now has made the rat
shy of steel traps, he prepares

00:24:45.740 --> 00:24:51.120
expanded-trigger wood traps and places them
in the rat runs and near food.

00:24:55.160 --> 00:24:58.220
A rat is caught; probably the last rat.

00:25:02.460 --> 00:25:07.980
Tracking patches are resmoothed and observed
daily for five days.

00:25:15.080 --> 00:25:21.440
Since no rat footprints are found, the storage
basement is considered to be rat-free.

00:25:21.450 --> 00:25:28.350
Thereafter, as in all rat-free premises, inspection
must be made at regular intervals.

00:25:28.350 --> 00:25:32.510
For this purpose, tracking patches laid in
dark, out-of-the-way places

00:25:32.510 --> 00:25:35.590
provide a permanent inspection record.

00:25:37.980 --> 00:25:43.420
There are other types of rodenticides and
as time goes on, more will be developed.

00:25:49.220 --> 00:25:55.639
But regardless of the rodenticide used, safety
for human beings and small animals,

00:25:55.639 --> 00:25:59.159
as well as effectiveness against rats, must
be considered.

00:26:00.180 --> 00:26:04.440
For greater safety, an emetic can be added
to many rodenticides.

00:26:05.240 --> 00:26:10.200
Dangerous poisons with which emetics cannot
be used should be handled

00:26:10.200 --> 00:26:17.180
only by qualified personnel under conditions that present no peril to human beings or domestic animals.

00:26:18.450 --> 00:26:22.750
By observing proper rat-killing techniques, ratproof premises

00:26:22.750 --> 00:26:27.529
can be completely freed of rats and kept that
way.

00:26:32.100 --> 00:26:38.160
Rat-killing by itself, without sanitation
or ratproofing, must often be used

00:26:38.169 --> 00:26:41.260
as a temporary, emergency measure.

00:26:41.260 --> 00:26:44.650
In sub-standard areas, there are conditions
like these:

00:26:44.650 --> 00:26:48.850
garbage, rubbish, rat food, and harborage
everywhere.

00:26:48.850 --> 00:26:51.710
Sanitation appears to be unknown.

00:26:56.360 --> 00:27:01.020
Obviously, under such conditions ratproofing
is impossible.

00:27:01.029 --> 00:27:05.549
Financial help may be needed to improve or
rebuild the sections.

00:27:05.549 --> 00:27:09.849
Individual and collective efforts to clean
the place up may take a long time.

00:27:13.160 --> 00:27:15.840
Everywhere there is evidence of rat infestation,

00:27:15.840 --> 00:27:20.480
carrying with it a constant danger of rat-borne
disease.

00:27:20.480 --> 00:27:24.820
There have been several reported cases of
children being bitten by rats.

00:27:28.300 --> 00:27:32.240
The health officer and sanitary engineer are
faced with a real problem.

00:27:32.990 --> 00:27:36.929
According to latest health inspection reports, three blocks in the area

00:27:36.929 --> 00:27:41.029
have the highest incidence of rat bites in
the entire city.

00:27:41.660 --> 00:27:46.240
A survey has shown that the same three blocks
are in the center of a large area

00:27:46.240 --> 00:27:48.540
that is heavily rat-infested.

00:27:48.680 --> 00:27:52.900
Poisoning operations are planned for this
area.

00:27:55.490 --> 00:28:02.490
The first rodenticide to be used is red squill, the safest rat poison known for residential areas.

00:28:02.490 --> 00:28:09.509
Four baits are selected; fresh fish, fresh
horse meat, rolled oats, and scratch feed.

00:28:09.509 --> 00:28:14.120
Each type of poison bait will be prepared
in torpedoes wrapped in a different color paper.

00:28:15.460 --> 00:28:19.960
After preparation, the four types of torpedoes are assembled into one pile.

00:28:32.060 --> 00:28:36.140
Then they are thoroughly intermingled, so
that when they are distributed,

00:28:36.140 --> 00:28:38.320
the rats will have a complete choice of baits.

00:28:44.820 --> 00:28:47.300
The assortment is loaded into carrying bags.

00:29:17.920 --> 00:29:22.780
To take full advantage of rat habits, poisoning is planned on a block-by-block basis.

00:29:23.780 --> 00:29:25.880
The men form a working team.

00:29:25.880 --> 00:29:29.780
Each man is assigned a section of the area
to cover.

00:29:35.580 --> 00:29:39.440
In any such program, the goodwill and cooperation
of the residents

00:29:39.840 --> 00:29:41.560
is an essential factor.

00:29:46.880 --> 00:29:50.750
The men must inform the occupants of the purpose
of the work and request them

00:29:50.750 --> 00:29:56.600
to confine pets and not to allow children
to molest the poison baits.

00:29:56.600 --> 00:30:01.690
Of course with native populations, consideration
must be given to their food habits,

00:30:01.690 --> 00:30:06.570
and no baits used which might be eaten under
the compulsion of hunger.

00:30:06.570 --> 00:30:10.590
The eradicator then proceeds to look for rat
signs.

00:30:10.590 --> 00:30:16.549
At places where he sees rat signs, he deposits
clusters of the four baits.

00:30:16.549 --> 00:30:18.640
The occupant of each house is contacted.

00:30:18.640 --> 00:30:24.000
The work is explained and consent obtained
for placing the baits.

00:30:24.100 --> 00:30:29.660
Experienced rat-control men quickly pick out
rat signs and place the bait accordingly.

00:30:31.100 --> 00:30:37.200
Active burrows and signs of gnawing indicate
the need for a generous supply of poison.

00:30:47.960 --> 00:30:51.500
Here's a place for many rats.

00:31:00.830 --> 00:31:04.770
Rubbish piles are logical places to expect
rat infestation.

00:31:09.960 --> 00:31:15.379
Hedgerows and shrubbery are usually honeycombed with rat runs.

00:31:15.379 --> 00:31:18.299
The area is thoroughly covered.

00:31:18.299 --> 00:31:22.179
Bait is much less expensive than labor and
should be used generously.

00:31:24.800 --> 00:31:28.100
At dusk the efforts begin to bear fruit.

00:31:28.110 --> 00:31:31.730
The maximum kill is almost always achieved
on the first attempt.

00:31:39.020 --> 00:31:45.100
Rats surviving the initial poisoning will
become suspicious and avoid the poisoned bait.

00:31:45.110 --> 00:31:48.890
This initial area of poisoning, therefore,
must be thorough.

00:31:50.540 --> 00:31:55.440
Not only must the dwelling areas be covered,
but the surrounding territory also.

00:31:57.340 --> 00:32:02.800
Poisoning must be extended to adjoining, open
areas that are reservoirs of rat infestation.

00:32:09.080 --> 00:32:15.180
Poison baits are distributed systematically,
block by block, until the entire area is treated.

00:32:17.080 --> 00:32:20.760
After a week, an inspection is made of the
area.

00:32:20.760 --> 00:32:25.200
Reports are collected on the results of the
poisoning program.

00:32:26.900 --> 00:32:32.519
Reports show that results were satisfactory
in more than 90 percent of the blocks treated.

00:32:32.519 --> 00:32:37.360
The remaining areas must be treated again.

00:32:50.649 --> 00:32:55.539
For the re-poisoning, zinc phosphide is used with tartar emetic added.

00:32:56.120 --> 00:33:00.000
A new group of materials will be mixed with
the poison.

00:33:00.009 --> 00:33:03.000
This time it is mixed with cubed apples.

00:33:03.720 --> 00:33:09.120
Zinc phosphide causes gastrointestinal irritation,
cerebral involvement,

00:33:09.129 --> 00:33:14.070
and liver injury, usually causing death within
12 hours.

00:33:14.070 --> 00:33:17.910
As always, the poison is carefully measured
out.

00:33:27.140 --> 00:33:31.380
In re-poisoning, each step must be repeated.

00:33:31.380 --> 00:33:35.040
The change in rodenticides is explained to
all householders,

00:33:35.040 --> 00:33:39.440
and the safety factor in the tartar emetic
is pointed out.

00:33:39.440 --> 00:33:44.409
The men work swiftly but carefully, seeking
out rat signs and distributing

00:33:44.409 --> 00:33:48.309
a generous supply of the poisoned bait.

00:33:48.309 --> 00:33:52.100
The re-poisoning was successful and accomplished
with temporary control

00:33:52.100 --> 00:33:59.460
sought through area poisoning, but much remains
to be done.

00:33:59.460 --> 00:34:02.940
In order for the beneficial effects to last
as long as possible,

00:34:02.940 --> 00:34:07.870
the inspector must instruct householders on
how to cut down available rat food

00:34:07.870 --> 00:34:11.070
and to remove rat harborages.

00:34:11.140 --> 00:34:17.060
Education and enforcement in sanitation must
be constant and progressive.

00:34:17.060 --> 00:34:20.870
The inspector studies the evidence of rat
infestation on each premise

00:34:20.870 --> 00:34:23.070
before contacting the occupant.

00:34:23.070 --> 00:34:28.250
Thus, he will be able to make specific suggestions
on solving the particular problems

00:34:28.250 --> 00:34:30.330
of each premise.

00:34:30.330 --> 00:34:36.070
One successful device in this educational
work is to tag inadequate garbage cans

00:34:36.070 --> 00:34:39.780
to emphasize to the owner that replacement is required.

00:34:41.580 --> 00:34:47.540
A specific suggestion might be the removal
of a board fence or elimination of shrubbery

00:34:47.550 --> 00:34:50.140
giving the rats access to open windows.

00:34:50.720 --> 00:34:55.640
A courteous and constructive approach to the
residents will usually evoke interest

00:34:55.650 --> 00:34:58.810
and full cooperation.

00:35:08.980 --> 00:35:13.660
Several weeks later, three blocks out of 41
originally poisoned

00:35:13.800 --> 00:35:17.820
require additional treatment and are scheduled for re-poisoning.

00:35:21.470 --> 00:35:25.830
To keep down the rat population in substandard
areas is a never-ending job,

00:35:25.830 --> 00:35:30.870
as long as environmental conditions make
available the basic requirements

00:35:30.870 --> 00:35:34.350
for rat life; namely food and harborage.

00:35:35.040 --> 00:35:40.380
In the long run, substandard housing must
be eliminated, and new construction

00:35:40.380 --> 00:35:44.750
of rat-proof design provided.

00:35:44.750 --> 00:35:51.260
[Music]

00:35:51.260 --> 00:35:58.110
When sanitary practices become habitual, depriving
rats of their food supply,

00:35:58.110 --> 00:36:03.080
when ratproof buildings are erected, and maintained
in good repair,

00:36:03.080 --> 00:36:05.760
reducing rat harborage,

00:36:05.760 --> 00:36:14.880
then, rat-killing becomes the final and conclusive measure in an integrated program of rat control.

00:36:14.880 --> 00:36:27.000
[Music]

